---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Rule from "../components/Rule.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import c from "../data/corrections.json";
const rows = c.rows;
const causes = c.causes;
const counted = Object.keys(causes)
  .map(k => [k, rows.filter(r => r[3] === k).length])
  .sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1]);
const label = { population: "A list mistaken for a population", scope: "A part searched, reported as the whole",
  circular: "A fact cited back to itself", tree: "The tree repeated before it was tested",
  reading: "A document read past what it says", process: "The archive's own working" };
---
<Base title="What was taken back"
      eyebrow={`${rows.length} corrections, and why each happened`}
      dek="Every claim this archive has published and then withdrawn, in one place, with the cause named. Nothing here has been quietly edited away: each of these sentences was on the site, and some of them were on it for weeks.">

<section class="blk">
  <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>A family history that only shows its conclusions is asking to be believed on trust. This one has
      been wrong nineteen times, and the corrections are more useful than most of the findings, because
      they are the only part of the site that says anything about <b>how the work goes wrong</b>.</p>
    <p>The right-hand column is the point. Sort by it and a pattern appears that no single correction
      would have shown.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:20px">
    {counted.map(([k, n]) => (
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="lab">{n} {n === 1 ? "time" : "times"}</div>
        <h3 style="margin:6px 0 8px;font-size:17px">{label[k]}</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;margin:0">{causes[k]}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

<Rule name="awl" label="One at a time" />

<section class="blk">
  <h2>The list</h2>
  <div class="panel" style="margin-top:16px">
    <label for="q" style="display:block;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:8px">
      <strong>Filter</strong> — a name, a year, a word from any of them</label>
    <input id="q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Start typing…"
           style="width:100%;padding:11px 13px;font-size:16px;font-family:inherit;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:3px;background:var(--ground);color:inherit" />
    <div style="margin-top:12px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px">
      <button class="fbtn on" data-f="">All <span class="m">{rows.length}</span></button>
      {counted.map(([k, n]) => (<button class="fbtn" data-f={k}>{label[k]} <span class="m">{n}</span></button>))}
    </div>
    <p id="count" class="cap" style="margin:12px 0 0" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="scroll">
    <table id="ctable">
      <thead><tr>
        <th class="m" style="width:7rem">Published</th>
        <th style="width:20rem">What it said</th>
        <th>What replaced it</th>
        <th style="width:13rem">Cause</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map(([d, was, now, cause, href]) => (
          <tr data-cause={cause} data-hay={[d, was, now, label[cause]].join(" ").toLowerCase()}>
            <td class="m">{d}</td>
            <td><b>&ldquo;{was}&rdquo;</b></td>
            <td>{now} {href && <a href={u(href)}>&rarr;</a>}</td>
            <td class="cap">{label[cause]}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>What the pattern says</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p><b>Three of the nineteen are the same mistake, and it is the one worth naming.</b> The archive
      searched what it happened to have, found nothing, and reported the absence as a fact about the
      world. <em>"Not one miner among them"</em> came from six occupations. <em>"The one time the form
      worked"</em> came from five death notices. <em>"They are not this family"</em> came from a
      geography the archive had never actually tested.</p>
    <blockquote>A list is not a population. Every negative on this site now carries the scope it was run
      over, and where the scope is small the page says so.
      <a href={u("/searched/")}>What was searched &rarr;</a></blockquote>
    <p>Three more were the reverse: a search run over part of the ground and written up as the whole.
      One province out of nine. Twenty-two documents out of forty-two. A register that turned out to
      cover a different colony entirely.</p>
    <p>And one, the most recent, is the worst kind: <b>a fact this archive manufactured from a reference
      number and then quoted back to itself.</b> An estate file numbered O/2899 was dated 1885; the
      archive wrote 1885 into a man's life as a death date, and then cited the death date as though it
      were evidence for the attribution. <a href={u("/documents/#o2899")}>How that unwound &rarr;</a></p>
    <p class="cap">Every correction is also in <a href={u("/research-log/")}>the research log</a>, in the order it
      happened, with what was being worked on at the time.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
(function () {
  var q = document.getElementById("q"), out = document.getElementById("count");
  if (!q) return;
  var rows = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll("#ctable tbody tr"));
  var btns = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll(".fbtn"));
  var filter = "";
  function run() {
    var v = q.value.trim().toLowerCase(), n = 0;
    for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
      var hit = (!v || rows[i].getAttribute("data-hay").indexOf(v) > -1) &&
                (!filter || rows[i].getAttribute("data-cause") === filter);
      rows[i].hidden = !hit;
      if (hit) n++;
    }
    out.textContent = n + (n === 1 ? " correction shown" : " corrections shown");
  }
  q.addEventListener("input", run);
  btns.forEach(function (b) {
    b.addEventListener("click", function () {
      btns.forEach(function (x) { x.classList.remove("on"); });
      b.classList.add("on");
      filter = b.getAttribute("data-f");
      run();
    });
  });
  run();
})();
</script>
</Base>
